      A.b.c←1
      A['d']←"ddd"
      A
.b: □
.b.c: 1

.d: ┌→──┐
    │ddd│
    └───┘

      A['d']←"def"
      A
.b: □
.b.c: 1

.d: ┌→──┐
    │def│
    └───┘


      Q←2 2⍴'a' 'leaf-a' 'bb' 'leaf-bb'
      Q
 a  leaf-a  
 bb leaf-bb 

      W←38 ⎕CR Q   ⍝ member names in Q are sorted, but 38 ⎕CR hashes them
                   ⍝ internally -- print_members() re-sorts by name for
                   ⍝ display regardless, so W still prints alphabetically.
      W
.a:  ┌→─────┐
     │leaf-a│
     └──────┘

.bb: ┌→──────┐
     │leaf-bb│
     └───────┘

      R←39 ⎕CR W
      R
 bb leaf-bb 
 a  leaf-a  

      ⍝ 38 ⎕CR turns scalar chars in Q into 1-element vector chars in W
      R1←R[⍋R[;1];]   ⍝ R1 is R with member names sorted
      R1 ≡ (,¨Q)
1

      )ERASE A

