      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #23): the identity fast paths
      ⍝ of ⌽ (scalar), 0⌽/0⊖, ⍉ (scalar/vector, and identity dyadic ⍉)
      ⍝ return their argument ALIASED (CLONE() under the active
      ⍝ NEW_CLONE scheme is not a real copy, just a new Value_P handle
      ⍝ on the SAME Value object), so Value::set_lval_bare_member_ref()'s
      ⍝ marker on a bare member reference like ZZ56S.a survived the
      ⍝ "selecting" function unbroken and was wrongly rejected by
      ⍝ Value::assign_cellrefs()'s bare-member SYNTAX ERROR -- even
      ⍝ though the error text itself names exactly this form
      ⍝ ((⌽S.member)←B) as the correct way to do it. Fixed by
      ⍝ Value::clear_lval_markers(), called at each aliasing identity
      ⍝ fast path (see Bif_F12_ROTATE.cc/Bif_F12_TRANSPOSE.cc/
      ⍝ Bif_F12_TAKE_DROP.cc/Bif_F12_COMMA.cc).
      ⍝
      ZZ56S.a←5
      (⌽ZZ56S.a)←7
      ZZ56S.a
7

      ZZ56S.a←1 2 3
      (0⌽ZZ56S.a)←9 8 7
      ZZ56S.a
9 8 7

      ZZ56S.a←1 2 3
      (⍉ZZ56S.a)←9 8 7
      ZZ56S.a
9 8 7

      ⍝ control: a genuinely non-identity application still worked even
      ⍝ before this fix (Bugs30 #14 only promised this much)
      ⍝
      ZZ56S.a←1 2 3
      (⌽ZZ56S.a)←9 8 7
      ZZ56S.a
7 8 9

